WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.059
The day my life changed began like any other day.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.223
I stayed home and watched our slave Sofia prepare lunch.

3
00:00:08.224 --> 00:00:12.016
Pompeii was a rich city near the mountain Vesuvius.

4
00:00:12.017 --> 00:00:16.166
Most families in Pompeii had three to five slaves.

5
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:21.148
Our slaves were treated like family, and Sofia was my best friend.

6
00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:26.455
My mother was at the market selling fish, and my father and brothers were fishing.

7
00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:32.086
A little before noon, Sofia and I took lunch to my mother.

8
00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:41.058
The market was crowded, and I didn't want to stay there, so I said, "Mom, Sofia and I will take lunch to Father and my brothers."

9
00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:47.489
My mother looked at me and said, "Go. We're almost finished here."

10
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:52.230
Sofia and I left. We were both happy to be free of the city.

11
00:00:52.231 --> 00:00:59.225
We walked through the Gate of Neptune and bowed to the god.

12
00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:02.179
It was a short walk from the gate to the marina.

13
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:10.650
My father's boat wasn't there, so Sofia and I sat on the dock and soaked our feet in the cool waters of the Mediterranean.

14
00:01:10.651 --> 00:01:19.259
Sofia shaded her eyes with one hand and suddenly shouted, "There's your father!"

15
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:27.453
Sofia and I waited on my father and brothers as they ate, while three slaves took the fish off my father's boat.

16
00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:30.393
"How was the catch?" I asked my father.

17
00:01:30.394 --> 00:01:34.734
"Fair," he replied.

18
00:01:34.735 --> 00:01:39.824
"It's so hot," I said. "I don't want to go back to the city."

19
00:01:39.825 --> 00:01:46.632
"Let's take the boat out and go for a swim in the cooler, deeper water," my brother suggested.

20
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:49.027
"Can we?" I asked my father.

21
00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:57.188
My father could never say no to me, since I was his youngest and his favorite.

22
00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:00.021
He looked at me and then at my brother.

23
00:02:00.022 --> 00:02:06.444
"Marcus Octavius, you can take Julia and Sofia out, but no fooling around.

24
00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:09.274
I expect you to be back by sunset."

25
00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:11.621
"Thank you, Father," I said.

26
00:02:11.622 --> 00:02:15.118
My brother took us out into the Bay of Naples.

27
00:02:15.119 --> 00:02:21.335
The coastline was beautiful in the sunshine.

28
00:02:21.336 --> 00:02:25.545
My brother dropped the anchor and said, "Let's swim!"

29
00:02:25.546 --> 00:02:29.272
He dove in and then Sofia and I followed.

30
00:02:29.273 --> 00:02:32.424
The water was refreshing and cool.

31
00:02:32.425 --> 00:02:40.926
As we were splashing and playing in the water, we heard a thunderous roar, and the sky became dark.

32
00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:44.593
We couldn't see anything; day had become night.

33
00:02:44.594 --> 00:02:50.543
My brother climbed back into the boat, and he helped Sofia and me get in.

34
00:02:50.544 --> 00:02:57.957
My brother was a good sailor, so he knew where to go even though we couldn't see.

35
00:02:57.958 --> 00:03:02.305
As we got closer to shore, it became harder to breathe.

36
00:03:02.306 --> 00:03:06.402
The air was filled with dust and bad-smelling gases.

37
00:03:06.403 --> 00:03:15.646
We could also see large flaming rocks shooting out of the mountain and a river of red flowing down its side.

38
00:03:15.647 --> 00:03:18.781
Sofia and I held each other and watched.

39
00:03:18.782 --> 00:03:23.033
My brother said, "It's gone! It's all gone!

40
00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:28.127
The marina, the city, our home—it's all gone," he cried out.

41
00:03:28.128 --> 00:03:30.692
"How can you tell?" I asked.

42
00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:36.106
"It all looks so strange, like some awful dream."

43
00:03:36.107 --> 00:03:39.313
"It's gone," he said quietly.

44
00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:46.786
"I use Mount Vesuvius as a guide, but half the mountain is missing, and our city has gone with it."

45
00:03:46.787 --> 00:03:49.431
I held Sofia tighter and cried.

46
00:03:49.432 --> 00:03:53.055
It seemed like it was the end of the world.

47
00:03:53.056 --> 00:03:56.112
My brother turned the boat back out to sea.

48
00:03:56.113 --> 00:04:03.950
The next day, we landed in Sorrento with Vesuvius still smoking and flaming in the background.

49
00:04:03.951 --> 00:04:07.259
Our city was gone, but we remained.

50
00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.883
My brother married Sofia and continued to fish.

51
00:04:10.884 --> 00:04:18.492
I married a lemon merchant from Sorrento, but I never forgot the last day of Pompeii.

52
00:04:18.493 --> 00:04:23.747
Mount Vesuvius erupted on August 24, 79 AD.

53
00:04:23.748 --> 00:04:29.229
It destroyed Pompeii and killed most of the twenty thousand people who lived there.

54
00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:36.959
The city disappeared, buried under seven to eight meters of dust, rock, and ash.

55
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:47.276
After 1,700 years Pompeii was rediscovered, and many of its buildings, monuments, and houses were uncovered and restored.

56
00:04:47.277 --> 00:04:50.696
Today it is a famous tourist attraction.

57
00:04:50.697 --> 00:04:57.700
Pompeii is a reminder to us all of the power of nature.

